#: src/PageHelp.php:49
msgid ""
"The information security management system dashboard: risks, controls, "
"incidents, deadlines and reviews at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:54
msgid ""
"Click a card to open the matching list. The dashboard menu lets you add or "
"move cards, and share it with other profiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:61
msgid ""
"The cyber maturity score (0 to 100): an overview of the progress of your "
"security management system, computed from your data."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:66
msgid ""
"Present it in management reviews; the calculation details show which "
"components to improve first."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:74
msgid ""
"Rates each applicable control of the Statement of Applicability on a scale "
"from 0 (non-existent) to 5 (optimised): the level reached today and the "
"level aimed for, with a target date. The gaps between the two make up the "
"security roadmap, and two dated campaigns show the progress. These optional "
"levels change neither the implementation status of the controls nor the "
"maturity score."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:82
msgid ""
"Create a campaign (for example once a year), fill in the current and target "
"levels of each control with a justification and an owner, then open the "
"\"Gaps\" tab: create an action for the largest gaps and download the report "
"for the management review. The next campaign takes over the targets of this "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:88
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clauses 6.2, 9.3 and 10.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:93
msgid ""
"For each control of the Statement of Applicability, this page lists what "
"prevents it from being compliant: failing automated check, missing or "
"expired evidence, policy not approved, effectiveness test overdue or "
"ineffective, open nonconformity, expired waiver."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:99
msgid ""
"Sort by severity and start with the most blocked controls. Click a control "
"to see its blockers, then click a blocker to open the screen where it is "
"fixed. The page is computed again each time and only shows what you are "
"allowed to read. Nothing is changed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:104
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001:2022 clause 9.1 and control A.5.36."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:109
msgid ""
"Before an audit, this page gathers the inconsistencies of your security "
"management system: risks without an owner, controls without evidence, "
"expired evidence, policies not reviewed, nonconformities closed without "
"action, and more."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:115
msgid ""
"Start with the high severity gaps. Click an item to open it, fix it, then "
"come back: the page is computed again each time. Nothing is changed "
"automatically. Export the list (CSV or PDF) to follow the preparation of the "
"audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:124
msgid ""
"At each surveillance audit, the certification body checks that the findings "
"of its previous audit have been dealt with. This page lists those findings "
"(nonconformities, areas of concern, opportunities for improvement) with "
"their corrective action, their evidence and whether they are lifted."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:131
msgid ""
"Record each certification audit with its type, then its findings in the "
"Findings tab of the audit, with the reference given by the body. Treat each "
"finding (cause, action, owner, due date, evidence in the Documents tab) "
"until it is verified. Export the PDF and hand it to the auditor at the "
"opening meeting of the next audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:141
msgid ""
"The certification body samples the processes of your security management "
"system over its three-year cycle: it does not audit them all every year. "
"This page copies its sampling programme (processes in rows, years in "
"columns) and, for the audit of the year, lists the sampled processes with "
"their previous findings and the screens to prepare."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:148
msgid ""
"Record each certification audit of the cycle with its planned date. Then "
"tick, in the column of each audit, the processes announced by the audit plan "
"of the body, and save. Before the audit, go through each sampled process: "
"lift its previous findings and check the controls and registers it relies "
"on. The processes are those of the internal audit programme (ISMS activities "
"of the responsibility matrix)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:156
msgid ""
"ISO/IEC 27006-1 (certification audit programme), ISO/IEC 27001 clause 9.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:163
msgid ""
"This page guides you, step by step, from setting up your security management "
"system to the certification audit: for each step, it shows what is expected, "
"where you stand according to the data already entered, and the screen to "
"open to complete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:169
msgid ""
"Follow the steps in order, starting with the one marked as the next step. "
"Click its button to open the screen concerned, complete it, then come back: "
"the page is computed again each time. Nothing is changed automatically. Give "
"the target date of the audit (or plan the certification audit): each step "
"not done gets an advised deadline, shown in the compliance calendar, and the "
"owner is warned when one risks being late. Export the PDF readiness report "
"to share where you stand."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:180
msgid ""
"Everything waiting for you in the security management system, on one page "
"and sorted by due date."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:184
msgid ""
"Start with the overdue items highlighted in red, then open each line to act "
"on it. The number next to the menu entry counts these items."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:192
msgid ""
"The documents an audit is waiting for from you: each request says what is "
"expected, for which control and by when."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:197
msgid ""
"Add the files (or an existing evidence of the control) to each request, then "
"submit it to the audit. If the audit asks you to complete a request, its "
"reason is shown in red."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:201
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 9.2 (internal audit)"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:205
msgid ""
"The audits you have been given access to, in read only: controls, progress, "
"submitted evidence and findings."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:210
msgid ""
"Open an audit, then download the submitted documents. Every download is "
"recorded. Your access ends on the date set by the organisation."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:218
msgid ""
"The register of all the contracts with ICT third-party service providers "
"that DORA requires: contracts, providers and their subcontractors, functions "
"supported and their criticality, data locations, substitutability and exit "
"plans. It is built from GLPI contracts, suppliers and business processes."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:225
msgid ""
"Fill in the financial entity below, then add each ICT contract from its "
"\"DORA register\" tab and complete the missing fields listed here. When "
"nothing is missing, download the templates and give them to your reporting "
"tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:230
msgid "DORA, article 28(3); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2956"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:234
msgid ""
"Assessment by framework: for each enabled framework, how many of its "
"controls are implemented, how many are proven by valid evidence, and the "
"resulting score."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:239
msgid ""
"Open the gaps of a framework, then update each control or attach the missing "
"evidence; an expired document no longer counts. Present the scores at the "
"management review."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:243
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1 and 9.3; mapping of each framework to Annex A"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:247
msgid ""
"Automated technical checks: checks computed from GLPI data (antivirus, disk "
"encryption, inventory, change validation, accounts), with a score per "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:252
msgid ""
"Review the gaps of each check and create the remediation ticket; once the "
"items are fixed, the score goes up. Present the scores at the management "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:256
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1; NIS2, article 21; GDPR, article 32"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:260
msgid ""
"Crisis exercises: simulate an incident (ransomware, data leak, outage) to "
"check that the team knows how to react and that the continuity plan works."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:265
msgid ""
"Start a scenario: a fictitious \"EXERCISE\" incident is created with one "
"task per step. In the crisis room, tick each step as soon as it is done; at "
"the end, the report measures reaction times and serves as audit evidence. At "
"least one exercise per year."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:270
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29 and 5.30"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:274
msgid ""
"The information security risk register: each risk is assessed (likelihood × "
"impact), linked to the assets it threatens and to the controls that reduce "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:279
msgid ""
"Identify risks, assess them, decide on a treatment (reduce, accept, "
"transfer, avoid) and set a review date. The owner is notified when it is due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:283
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.2 and 6.1.3; 8.2 and 8.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:288
msgid ""
"Bring an existing risk register kept in a spreadsheet into the plugin, and "
"take it back out in the same format."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:293
msgid ""
"Download the template or export the register, fill it in, then analyse the "
"file: nothing is saved before you have read the report and confirmed. "
"Importing the same file again updates the risks without duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:298
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.2 and 8.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:302
msgid ""
"The risk heat map: how risks are spread by likelihood and impact, to see at "
"a glance where high risks are concentrated."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:307
msgid "Use it in management reviews; click a cell to open the matching risks."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:313
msgid ""
"The risk appetite and tolerance set by management for each risk category, "
"and the open risks that exceed them."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:318
msgid ""
"Have management approve the levels; then give each risk above the appetite a "
"treatment or a formal, justified acceptance. Risks above tolerance come "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:322
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.2; ISO 31000, 6.3.4"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:326
msgid ""
"Key risk indicators (KRI): values measured over time, entered by hand or "
"measured every day from technical checks, fleet vulnerabilities and the risk "
"register, with orange and red thresholds."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:332
msgid ""
"Set the thresholds of each indicator, enter the manual values at each "
"review, and open a ticket for any indicator in the red."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:336
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.2 and 9.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:340
msgid ""
"Typical infrastructure risks (exposed administration service, flat network, "
"poorly isolated guest Wi-Fi...), ready to be added to the register."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:345
msgid ""
"Tick those that apply to you and import them, then assess them in the "
"register. Nothing is imported without your choice."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:352
msgid ""
"Risks related to your suppliers and service providers: dependency, access to "
"your data, security of their services."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:357
msgid ""
"Create one risk per important supplier, evaluate it with one or more "
"questionnaires (Questionnaires tab), follow its contracts and the \"Security "
"watch\" tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:361
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.19 to 5.22"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:365
msgid ""
"The Statement of Applicability (SoA): the 93 Annex A controls, each declared "
"applicable or not, with its justification and implementation status."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:370
msgid ""
"For each control, state whether it applies, why, and how far its "
"implementation has progressed. Then have the SoA approved."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:374
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.3 d)"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:379
msgid ""
"The security policies awaiting your approval: read the frozen version, then "
"approve or reject it with a comment."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:384
msgid ""
"Answer each request; a rejection needs a comment so that the author can "
"correct the policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:387
msgid "ISO 27001, A.5.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:391
msgid ""
"Approved versions of the Statement of Applicability, with the approver and "
"the date."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:395
msgid ""
"Request approval after every significant change to the SoA; the approver "
"cannot be the requester."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:402
msgid ""
"The requirements of clauses 4 to 10 of the standard (context, leadership, "
"planning, support, operation, evaluation, improvement) and the evidence that "
"they are met."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:407
msgid ""
"For each requirement, state its status and attach or link the evidence "
"(document, review, procedure)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:411
msgid "ISO 27001, clauses 4 to 10"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:415
msgid ""
"Your legal, regulatory and contractual security obligations (GDPR, NIS2, "
"customer clauses...)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:419
msgid ""
"List them with their source and owner, and set a review date to check they "
"are still met."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:422
msgid "ISO 27001, 4.2; Annex A 5.31"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:426
msgid ""
"The record of processing activities required by the GDPR: one entry per "
"processing of personal data, with its purpose, legal basis, data, recipients "
"and retention periods."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:431
msgid ""
"Describe each processing, link the applications, assets and suppliers "
"involved, settle the gaps shown, review the register every year and export "
"it if the supervisory authority asks for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:436
msgid "GDPR, article 30; ISO 27001, Annex A 5.34"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:440
msgid ""
"Requests from people exercising their GDPR rights (access, rectification, "
"erasure...) and the deadline to answer each one: one month, or three when "
"the extension is justified."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:445
msgid ""
"Record each request on the day it arrives, answer before the deadline and "
"attach the proof. Put the identity of the person only in the Requester field."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:449
msgid "GDPR, articles 12 and 15 to 22"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:454
msgid ""
"Checks, from the software and licenses already recorded in GLPI, that the "
"organization respects the licenses it bought: commercial software installed "
"without any license, more installations than licensed seats, and expired "
"licenses still in use. Results are grouped by entity."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:461
msgid ""
"Check the list of watched publishers, then for each finding record the "
"missing license in GLPI, buy seats, uninstall the software or renew the "
"license. Export the list (CSV) for the auditor. Nothing is changed "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:466
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.32"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:471
msgid ""
"Shows, from the volumes reported by the GLPI inventory agent (BitLocker, "
"FileVault, LUKS, VeraCrypt...), which computers are fully encrypted, "
"partially encrypted, not encrypted or of unknown state, by entity, computer "
"type and location. Computers that must be encrypted and are not, or use a "
"weak algorithm, are gaps."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:478
msgid ""
"Choose which computers must be encrypted, encrypt the computers listed as "
"gaps, install the inventory agent on those of unknown state, and declare "
"where the recovery key is backed up. The plugin never reads nor stores any "
"recovery key. Record the result as an effectiveness test of the control to "
"keep the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:484
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.8.24 and A.8.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:489
msgid ""
"Keeps the results of the security audits of your Active Directory "
"(PingCastle, Purple Knight) and of the configuration of your Entra ID and "
"Microsoft 365 tenant (Maester, ScubaGear): the files that your team produces "
"are imported here, with the score and the rules or checks that failed. Each "
"one is linked to the ISO/IEC 27001 controls it concerns, and the history "
"shows how the score changes from one report to the next."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:497
msgid ""
"Run these tools regularly (for example every quarter), import each report, "
"then decide how to treat the rules: propose an action or a ticket for those "
"you fix, and follow the rules resolved by the next report. Nothing is "
"created automatically. The page is reserved to the sensitive registers right."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:503
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.15 to A.5.18, A.5.23, A.8.2 and A.8.5"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:508
msgid ""
"Shows, from the GLPI inventory (operating system, version, updates reported "
"by the agent), the date of the last known security patch of each computer "
"and whether it is within the target delay of its criticality. Computers "
"published on the Internet and critical computers come first, with the known "
"vulnerabilities of their system and their end of support."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:516
msgid ""
"Set the target delay of each criticality, classify the computers (C/I/A "
"tab), patch the late computers, and install the inventory agent on those of "
"unknown state. The page only reads the inventory: it starts no update. "
"Record the result as an effectiveness test of the control to keep the "
"evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:522
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.8.8 and A.8.19"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:527
msgid ""
"Shows who can access the Windows file shares: share and NTFS permissions "
"imported from each file server, accounts matched with the GLPI users and "
"groups, and the gaps an auditor looks for (everyone can modify, rights given "
"to a person, deleted or disabled accounts, broken inheritance, share without "
"an owner)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:534
msgid ""
"Run the PowerShell script provided on each file server (it only reads), "
"import the CSV file, classify the sensitive shares and designate an owner "
"for each one. The owner then reviews the rights of the share; the "
"administrator applies the changes on the server and the next import shows "
"the rights added and removed."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:540
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.15, A.5.18 and A.8.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:545
msgid ""
"Measures how well the configuration of the computers follows a hardening "
"guide (CIS, ANSSI, DISA STIG...), from the results files of the OpenSCAP "
"scanner: rate of rules passed per computer, change since the previous scan, "
"most frequent failed rules and history."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:551
msgid ""
"Scan the machines with OpenSCAP, import the results file (XCCDF or ARF), "
"match the results that are not matched to a computer, then fix the failed "
"rules, starting with the high severity ones. A remediation ticket can be "
"proposed for a computer: it is created only when you click. Nothing is "
"changed on the machines."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:557
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.8.9"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:562
msgid ""
"Shows which important assets send their logs to a log platform (Wazuh, "
"Graylog, Elastic or OpenSearch, Splunk, syslog), which send nothing or "
"nothing for several days, and whether each platform keeps the logs long "
"enough and synchronizes the clocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:568
msgid ""
"Choose the assets that must send their logs, import the list of hosts of "
"each log platform (or let the Wazuh plugin be read), connect the assets "
"listed as gaps, and declare the retention and the time server of each "
"platform. The page only reads: it runs nothing on the platforms. Record the "
"result as an effectiveness test of the control to keep the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:575
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.8.15, A.8.16 and A.8.17"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:579
msgid ""
"The context of the organization: the internal and external issues that "
"affect information security, and the interested parties with their "
"expectations and what the ISMS retains."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:584
msgid ""
"List the issues and the interested parties, decide for each one whether the "
"ISMS retains it, link the related risks, obligations and controls, answer "
"the climate change question, and review each item at least once a year. Use "
"the export of the list for the auditor."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:589
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clauses 4.1 and 4.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:594
msgid ""
"Shows, for each site (a location of GLPI), the last physical security "
"assessment: the state of each control A.7.1 to A.7.14 side by side, the "
"score, and when the site must be assessed again (at least once a year)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:600
msgid ""
"Assess each site: walk through it, record the state, the finding and the "
"evidence (photos, reports) of each control, and list its zones with their "
"access controls. Create an action for each partial or non-compliant control. "
"Link the physical security policy. Assess the site again before the date "
"shown."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:606
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.7.1 to A.7.14"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:611
msgid ""
"Shows whether each main IT operations activity (backup, restore, monitoring, "
"updates...) has a documented procedure that is approved and reviewed on "
"time, with its version, its owner and who has acknowledged it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:617
msgid ""
"For each domain without an up-to-date procedure, add one or update it: "
"attach the document, have it approved, set its next review date, then launch "
"the reading acknowledgement for the groups or profiles that carry it out. "
"Archive the register on control A.5.37 before an audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:623
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.37"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:628
msgid ""
"The applications developed or maintained in-house, with their secure "
"development practices (framework, code review, SAST, DAST and dependency "
"analyses, security requirements, architecture principles, outsourced "
"development, separated environments), and the releases of the last 12 months "
"with their security validation."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:635
msgid ""
"Fill in the \"Secure development\" tab of each application, link the changes "
"to their application, then have each release approved by the CIO or the CISO "
"in the \"Security release validation\" tab of the change, before it goes "
"into production."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:640
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.8.25 to A.8.31"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:645
msgid ""
"Who to contact outside the organization when something happens: authorities "
"(data protection authority, national CSIRT, police), regulators, insurers "
"and special interest groups, with their details, when to contact them, the "
"time limit and who is allowed to call them."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:651
msgid ""
"Record each official contact, tick the events (and, if needed, the types of "
"incident) for which it must be informed, verify the details at least once a "
"year, keep a printed copy of the register (PDF) for use during a crisis, and "
"archive it on controls A.5.5 and A.5.6 after each review."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:657
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.5 and A.5.6"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:661
msgid ""
"Who performs, approves, is consulted on or is informed of each activity of "
"the ISMS, with the GLPI users and groups. Conflicts of duties and missing "
"approvers are reported here."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:666
msgid ""
"For each activity, add who performs it and a single approver, mark the "
"sensitive activities, fix the alerts, then archive the matrix as evidence "
"before the audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:670
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 5.3 and control A.5.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:675
msgid ""
"The competences each ISMS function needs (CISO, DPO, administrator...), who "
"holds each function, what each person has acquired through passed trainings "
"or declared evidence, and the gaps."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:680
msgid ""
"Add the functions and their required competences with the expected level, "
"say who holds them, link the trainings that give each competence, declare "
"the certificates and diplomas, plan the proposed actions, then archive the "
"file as evidence before the audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:685 src/PageHelp.php:697 src/PageHelp.php:710
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 7.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:689
msgid ""
"The catalogue of the information security competences of the organization, "
"and the trainings that give each one once passed."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:694
msgid ""
"Describe each competence and link the trainings that give it, with the level "
"reached."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:701
msgid ""
"The competences acquired outside the trainings of the plugin, each one with "
"its evidence: certificate, diploma, annual review or proven experience."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:706
msgid ""
"Record the reference of the evidence, its date and its end of validity, and "
"attach the file in the Documents tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:714
msgid ""
"The register of personal data breaches: every breach is documented, whether "
"or not it was notified, with its facts, effects and the measures taken."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:719
msgid ""
"Record each breach as soon as it is known (from the security incident when "
"there is one), decide within 72 h whether to notify the supervisory "
"authority and write down why, decide whether to inform the people concerned, "
"then export the register when the authority asks for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:725
msgid "GDPR, articles 33 and 34"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:729
msgid ""
"The internal audit programme: scope, dates, auditors, report and findings."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:733
msgid ""
"Plan the year's audits, enter the report and the findings; each "
"nonconformity opens an action plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:737
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:742
msgid ""
"The internal audit programme over the certification cycle: which ISMS "
"process is audited which year, and which one is not covered yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:747
msgid ""
"Make sure every process is audited at least once over the cycle: plan an "
"audit for each process in red or orange, and choose its processes in the "
"\"Programme and independence\" tab of the audit."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:752
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.2.2; ISO 19011, 5"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:756
msgid ""
"Nonconformities and observations, with their corrective and preventive "
"actions (CAPA)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:760
msgid ""
"Analyse the cause, describe the corrective action, assign an owner and a due "
"date, then check its effectiveness before closing."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:764
msgid "ISO 27001, 10.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:768
msgid ""
"Security training and awareness sessions, with their participants and "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:772
msgid ""
"Record each session, its participants and its renewal date; a reminder is "
"sent when it is due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:775
msgid "ISO 27001, 7.2 and 7.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:780
msgid ""
"Phishing simulations: the fake phishing campaigns sent with an external tool "
"(GoPhish, a provider...), their results and the trend from one campaign to "
"the next. The plugin never sends any email."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:786
msgid ""
"Record each campaign (date, tool, scenario, targeted population), then "
"import the results file of the tool in the Results tab. Offer a remedial "
"training to the people who clicked. Inform the staff beforehand that "
"simulations take place, and delete the results per person once the follow-up "
"is done, or set a retention period in the configuration of the plugin. The "
"rates by group and by entity stay anonymous."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:793 src/PageHelp.php:806
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, clause 7.3 and control A.6.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:797
msgid ""
"Import of the results of a phishing simulation: each line of the file is "
"matched with a GLPI user by email address or login."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:802
msgid ""
"Check the column of each field, then import. The lines not matched are "
"listed on the campaign so that you can correct them."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:810
msgid ""
"Management reviews: the periodic review of the information security "
"management system by top management."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:815
msgid ""
"At least once a year, prepare the review (indicators, audits, incidents, "
"risks), record the decisions and the resulting actions."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:819
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.3"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:822
msgid "Security objectives and their indicators measured over time."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:824
msgid ""
"Define measurable objectives, enter the measurements each period and track "
"progress towards the target."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:828
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.2 and 9.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:832
msgid ""
"Access rights review campaigns: each manager confirms or removes the rights "
"of their team."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:836
msgid ""
"Start a campaign; managers decide line by line, helped by a suggestion "
"(keep, remove or examine) and its reason. Removing a right opens a ticket, "
"it is never applied automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:841
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.18"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:845
msgid ""
"Accounts to check: inactive accounts, accounts missing from the directory, "
"duplicates or never used."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:850
msgid ""
"Review the list and open a ticket for each account to disable; nothing is "
"disabled automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:858
msgid ""
"Security compliance of each person: screening, confidentiality agreement, "
"mandatory trainings, IT charter, security policies read, access review and "
"account hygiene."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:863
msgid ""
"Follow up the gaps with the person and their manager; nothing is changed "
"automatically. The deadline for newcomers and the weight of each component "
"are set in the plugin configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:868
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 6.1, 6.2, 6.3, 6.5, 6.6 and 5.18"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:872
msgid ""
"Periodic reviews (backups, logs, rights, continuity plan...) scheduled as "
"recurring tickets."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:876
msgid ""
"Enable the useful reviews and their frequency; a ticket is created at each "
"due date for the person in charge."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:883
msgid ""
"The matrix of authorised network flows: who talks to whom, on which port, "
"and why."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:887
msgid ""
"Describe each flow with its justification and owner, or import your firewall "
"export, then review the matrix regularly."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:891
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 8.20 to 8.22"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:895
msgid ""
"Work email addresses found in known data breaches (Have I Been Pwned), "
"checked every day."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:899
msgid ""
"For each new exposure, have the password changed (and enable multi-factor "
"authentication) if passwords were exposed, then mark it as handled."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:903
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.7 and 5.17"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:907
msgid ""
"The compliance calendar: all due dates (reviews, audits, renewals, "
"obligations) in one place, also visible in the GLPI planning."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:912
msgid ""
"Check it to anticipate due dates; subscribe your calendar with the iCal link."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:918
msgid ""
"One-off compliance events to add to the calendar (regulator inspection, "
"crisis exercise, contractual deadline...)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:923
msgid ""
"Add the event with its date and owner; it appears in the compliance calendar."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:929
msgid ""
"The library of security policies, versioned, with their approval and review "
"date."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:933
msgid ""
"Upload each policy, have it approved, distribute it and review it when due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:936
msgid "ISO 27001, 5.2; Annex A 5.1"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:940
msgid "Dated evidence (reports, attestations, certificates) and its validity."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:944
msgid ""
"State how long each piece of evidence is valid; a renewal ticket is opened "
"when it expires."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:951
msgid ""
"Prepare the evidence pack the auditor asks for: one ZIP archive per "
"perimeter, with the evidence of each control and each requirement, the "
"reports already archived and a PDF index that lists them with their date and "
"SHA-256 fingerprint."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:957
msgid ""
"Choose the perimeter and check its contents: renew expired evidence and "
"attach what is missing first. Then generate the pack and download it from "
"the list. Only what you can read is included; expired evidence is listed in "
"the index, not included. Nothing is changed in the registers."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:964
msgid ""
"ISO/IEC 27001, clauses 7.5.3 (control of documented information) and 9.2 "
"(internal audit)"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:970
msgid ""
"The effectiveness tests of the Annex A controls: a control in place is "
"checked to really work, with its method, result and evidence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:975
msgid ""
"Set a test plan on each control, record each test from the control's "
"\"Effectiveness tests\" tab and carry out the tests that are due first. An "
"ineffective control opens a non-conformity."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:980
msgid "ISO 27001, 9.1; ISO 27002, 5.35 and 5.36"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:984
msgid ""
"The audit log of the security incidents: who consulted or changed what, "
"when, with which profile and from which address, including impersonations."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:989
msgid ""
"Filter the entries, export them for an audit or a court, and check the "
"integrity regularly: each entry is sealed with the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:996
msgid ""
"Import of a CSV export of the alerts from an EDR or XDR console: each alert "
"becomes an incident with its indicators, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, hosts and "
"accounts."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1001
msgid ""
"Check the columns proposed, choose how to group the alerts, then import. An "
"alert already imported is ignored; the original lines are kept unchanged on "
"the incident."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1008
msgid ""
"EBIOS Risk Manager studies: the risk assessment method of ANSSI, the French "
"national cybersecurity agency, published under an open licence."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1013
msgid ""
"Create one study per scope, then work through its workshops in order: "
"business values and feared events, risk sources, stakeholders and strategic "
"scenarios, operational scenarios, then their treatment, which feeds the risk "
"register."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1021
msgid ""
"Remediation playbooks: the standard steps to follow for each type of "
"incident (ransomware, phishing, compromised account...)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1026
msgid ""
"Adapt the five playbooks provided to your context; from an incident, apply "
"one to get its plan of tasks. Mandatory steps must be done or marked not "
"applicable before closing."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1034
msgid ""
"Information security crisis scenarios of the continuity plan: ransomware, "
"data leak, compromise of privileged accounts, unavailability of a critical "
"supplier, denial of service. For each one: the processes it stops, how to "
"keep working without lowering security, who does what, and which playbook to "
"follow."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1041
msgid ""
"Add the default scenarios, then adapt each one: choose the impacted "
"processes, check the secure degraded mode and the roles, link the response "
"playbook. Every critical process should have a scenario, and every scenario "
"should be exercised at least once a year."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1046
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.29"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1051
msgid ""
"Crisis message templates: the messages prepared in advance for each kind of "
"crisis (major incident, personal data breach, unavailability, ransomware), "
"with the people and organizations to inform for each one."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1057
msgid ""
"Adapt the templates provided and fill in the distribution list of each one "
"(users, groups and official contacts). During a crisis, open the Crisis "
"communication tab of the incident: the message is filled in from the "
"incident, you send it yourself, then record it. The plugin never sends any "
"email."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1063
msgid "ISO/IEC 27001, control A.5.26 and clause 7.4"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1068
msgid ""
"Supplier questionnaire templates: the questions asked to your suppliers, "
"grouped by section, with their weight, the expected answer and the evidence "
"to provide. One template per need: information security, personal data, "
"artificial intelligence..."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1074
msgid ""
"Adapt the historical questionnaire or create your own templates, then start "
"an evaluation from the Questionnaires tab of a supplier risk. A supplier can "
"be evaluated with several templates; each evaluation keeps its score and its "
"history."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1080
msgid ""
"ISO/IEC 27001, controls A.5.19 to A.5.21; NIS2 art. 21(2)(d); DORA art. 28"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1087
msgid ""
"Custom frameworks: follow a framework that is not built in (group "
"requirements, sector or contractual framework, customer security plan) by "
"importing it from a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1092
msgid ""
"Download the template, fill in one line per requirement with the Annex A "
"controls that meet it, import it, then enable the framework. A new version "
"of the file updates it without losing the statuses already entered."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1100
msgid ""
"Coverage rules: which assets must have which document (for example, every "
"server must have its operations sheet)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1105
msgid ""
"Create one rule per requirement; the result lists the covered assets and "
"those to complete."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1111
msgid ""
"Security exemptions: accepted exceptions to a policy or a control, limited "
"in time and compensated."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1116
msgid ""
"Justify each exemption, describe the compensating measures, have it approved "
"and set its end date; it is reassessed when due."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1120
msgid "ISO 27001, 6.1.3; Annex A 5.36"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1124
msgid ""
"Business processes: who owns them, how critical they are, how long they can "
"be interrupted and which GLPI items they depend on."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1129
msgid ""
"For each process, rate the impact of an interruption over time (business "
"impact analysis), set its MTPD, RTO and RPO, and link the applications, "
"servers and suppliers it needs; items slower than the process are reported. "
"Export the result for your continuity plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1134
msgid "ISO 22301, 8.2.2; ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29 and 5.30"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1139
msgid ""
"Recovery test programme: when each business process was last tested, whether "
"the test met its RTO and RPO, and which processes are not tested in time."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1144
msgid ""
"Plan a test for each process reported as overdue or not tested this year, "
"then record the measured recovery time and data loss in its \"Recovery "
"strategy\" tab. Show this view to the auditor as evidence that ICT "
"continuity is tested regularly."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1149
msgid "ISO 22301, 8.5; ISO 27001, Annex A 5.30"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1153
msgid ""
"Single points of failure: critical items that depend on a single source, "
"according to GLPI's impact analysis."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1158
msgid ""
"Create the matching risk or add redundancy; export the list for your "
"business continuity plan."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1161
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.29, 5.30 and 8.14"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1164
msgid "The domino effect: how one incident or risk can lead to others."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1166
msgid ""
"Link items from the \"Domino effect\" tab of a risk or an incident; this "
"page shows the whole picture."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1173
msgid ""
"Security incidents: qualification, affected assets, CVEs, costs, regulatory "
"notifications (data protection authority, NIS2)."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1178
msgid ""
"Declare the incident, qualify it, follow up the actions and meet the "
"notification deadlines shown on the record."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1182
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 5.24 to 5.28"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1186
msgid ""
"Known vulnerabilities (CVEs) of the software installed on your fleet, with "
"their real-world exploitation (KEV, EPSS) and CERT-FR advisories."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1191
msgid ""
"Handle exploited and priority vulnerabilities first; open one update ticket "
"per software."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1194 src/PageHelp.php:1218
msgid "ISO 27001, Annex A 8.8"
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1198
msgid ""
"Fleet software to match with a CPE reference so that its vulnerabilities are "
"tracked."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1202
msgid ""
"Start with the most exposed (browsers, remote access, VPN): search for the "
"CPE, confirm it, or ignore software with no stakes."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1209
msgid ""
"The machines most exposed to the known vulnerabilities of their watched "
"software, operating system and firmware, to know where to start updating."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1214
msgid ""
"Handle the machines at the top of the list first; the \"Vulnerabilities\" "
"tab of each one details the CVEs and the update ticket."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1222
msgid ""
"The correlation catalogue: reference products, their CPEs and the names "
"under which they appear in the inventory."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1227
msgid ""
"It is filled from \"Software to watch\"; correct an alias or a CPE here if "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1233
msgid ""
"Mappings between Annex A and other frameworks, to reuse your work across "
"several standards."
msgstr ""

#: src/PageHelp.php:1236
msgid "Check the mappings before an audit against another framework."
msgstr ""

